---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service — Tee Shop">
	<div class="simple-page align-left">
		<h1>Terms of Service</h1>
		<p><em>Last updated: [date]. This is a starting draft, not legal advice — have it reviewed before relying on it.</em></p>

		<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
		<p>
			Tee Shop ("we", "us") is operated by [Your Business Legal Name], [business address].
			Contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>2. Orders and payment</h2>
		<p>
			Every item is made to order — nothing is printed until you buy it. Payments are processed
			securely by Stripe; we never see or store your full card number. Prices are shown in USD
			and charged at checkout.
		</p>

		<h2>3. Production and shipping</h2>
		<p>
			Because each item is printed after you order it, please allow a few business days for
			production in addition to shipping time. Shipping costs and timelines depend on your
			delivery address and are shown at checkout.
		</p>

		<h2>4. Returns and refunds</h2>
		<p>
			See our <a href={`${base}refund-policy`}>Refund &amp; Returns Policy</a> for details.
		</p>

		<h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
		<p>
			All designs, artwork, and site content are owned by us or our licensors. You may not
			reproduce or resell them without permission.
		</p>

		<h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
		<p>
			We provide this site and its products "as is." To the fullest extent permitted by law, we
			aren't liable for indirect or consequential damages arising from your use of the site or
			products purchased through it.
		</p>

		<h2>7. Changes to these terms</h2>
		<p>
			We may update these terms from time to time; the "last updated" date above will reflect
			the most recent revision.
		</p>

		<h2>8. Governing law</h2>
		<p>These terms are governed by the laws of [your jurisdiction].</p>

		<h2>9. Contact</h2>
		<p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com</a>.</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
